# Analysis outputs: regenerated by the analysis scripts, which, with the reports, are the record.
# analysis/out/data/README.md lists the few artefacts kept deliberately.
# The 2026-09-27 question-based reorganisation (analysis/REORG_LOG.md) renamed and regrouped
# analysis/scripts/ and analysis/out/reports/ but did not touch out/data|figures|logs/ (stage 3,
# not yet done) — these rules are depth-based and stay valid under the new script folder names.
analysis/out/data/
analysis/out/figures/
analysis/out/logs/

# Results written beside the scripts that produced them (some hold large image data).
analysis/scripts/*/out/

# Default output folders of the Figure 2 reproduction scripts when no --output-root is given.
manuscript-figures-notebook/figure2/outputs_*/

# The synthetic benchmark dataset shared by Figures 3 and 4. Its 120 meshes are tracked (they are
# the published input and cannot be regenerated bit for bit); this rule only stops a
# directory-level `git add` from sweeping in new files that appear beside them.
manuscript-figures-notebook/figure3/synthetic/dataset/

# Figure 4: the notebooks and pipeline code are tracked; image data and the collaborators' code are
# not. The tracked files of data_real/ were added explicitly; this rule keeps new files there out
# of a directory-level `git add`.
manuscript-figures-notebook/figure4/*.tif
manuscript-figures-notebook/figure4/*.tiff
manuscript-figures-notebook/figure4/**/*.tif
manuscript-figures-notebook/figure4/**/*.tiff
manuscript-figures-notebook/figure4/data_real/
manuscript-figures-notebook/figure4/Vertax_A549_EpithelialCell_Code/

# Written into the working directory by do_n_bilevel_optimization (save_folder defaults to ".").
hyper-parameters.txt
